From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:35:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: keep the chip's radar reports in debugfs

The chip's radar report (MCU_EXT_EVENT_RDD_REPORT) says what it saw: the
radar type it matched, which of its long, constant-PRF and staggered-PRF
detectors fired, the PRIs it measured, its pulse counters and up to 32
periodic, long and hardware pulses, each with its start, width and power.
mt7915_mcu_rx_radar_detected() passes the detection on to mac80211 (or
cfg80211, for the background chain), counts it in dfs_hw_pattern and
throws the rest away. So when radar takes a DFS channel away there is no
telling afterwards what the chip saw: a radar, or noise or a neighbour's
transmission it took for one.

Keep the last 8 reports, in a ring in mt7915_dev under a spinlock (the
event comes in the MCU rx path, debugfs reads in process context). Each is
numbered and has the real time and boottime it came at, the detector, the
band index of the radio the detector maps to and that radio's channel
(control channel, width and center_freq1; the background chain's own for
the background detector), then the report's fields and pulses in host
order. A new read-only debugfs file, rdd_reports, next to rdd_monitor,
prints them oldest first: a line per report, then a line per pulse
(periodic, long, then the hardware's), as space-separated key/value pairs
in decimal, in the chip's own units, the 16-bit power signed. A script on
the router parses it.

Only what the event carries is read: a report cut short reads as zero past
its end, and each pulse count is cut to 32 and to the pulses that arrived
whole. The detector index is checked too, which the handler read before
checking anything: an event too short to carry one is dropped with an
error, as an unknown detector's is. Reports the handler drops (an unknown
detector, no radio for it, too short) aren't kept. What reaches mac80211
and cfg80211 is unchanged.

mt7915_mcu2_events_rdd_report, _rdd_report_short, _rdd_report_ring and
_rdd_report_dropped, and mt7915_debugfs_test_rdd_reports for the format.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
